## Phase 2: Exam Taking Logic

I have implemented persistent, server-synced exam-taking logic that mirrors the premium experience of public exams.

### Changes Made

#### Core Logic
- **[NEW] [use-practice-exam-attempt.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/hooks/use-practice-exam-attempt.ts)**:
    - Created a custom hook to manage practice session state.
    - Synced answers with the server in real-time.
    - Provided performance metrics and answer states.

#### UI & Experience
- **[MODIFY] [mcq-practice-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/mcq-practice-service.tsx)**:
    - Integrated `createPracticeSession` mutation to persist sessions before starting.
    - Added conditional rendering for configuration and practice views.
- **[MODIFY] [take-mcq-practice-view.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/take-mcq-practice-view.tsx)**:
    - Refactored to use the new attempt hook.
    - Added **Audio Feedback** for correct/incorrect answers.
    - Added **Confetti Effects** for achieving streaks.
- **[NEW] [use-audio-feedback.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/hooks/use-audio-feedback.ts)**:
    - Added a hook for generating procedural audio feedback.

## Verification Results

### Session Persistence
Refreshing the page during a practice session correctly restores the state (answered questions) from the database.

### Interactive Feedback
Audio tones play immediately upon selection, and confetti triggers after a 5-question streak or when breaking a best streak.

### Final Submission
The submission flow correctly calculates final scores and marks the session as completed in the database.

